    {
      "tag": "div",
      "attributes": {
        "class": "view-mode-section view-mode-section__branch view-mode-section__branch--human"
      },
      "html": "<div class=\"w-full bg-chalk\"><section class=\"blog-reading-shell pointer-events-auto\" data-v-1c6297c3><nav class=\"blog-breadcrumb\" aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\"><a href=\"/feed\">Blogs</a><span aria-hidden=\"true\">/</span><span>SEO</span></nav><article aria-labelledby=\"blog-53-title\"><header class=\"blog-article-header\"><p class=\"blog-eyebrow\">Search &amp; AI Visibility</p><h1 id=\"blog-53-title\">What an SEO specialist should do beyond rankings</h1><p class=\"blog-article-summary\">Look for useful work across technical foundations, intent research, page improvements, implementation and business-aware reporting.</p><p class=\"blog-byline\">Fyntix Editorial · Updated <time datetime=\"2026-11-24\">24 Nov 2026</time> · 2 min read</p></header><nav class=\"blog-contents\" aria-label=\"On this page\"><p>On this page</p><ol><li><a href=\"#blog-53-section-1\">Understand the offer and audience</a></li><li><a href=\"#blog-53-section-2\">Review the technical and content foundations</a></li><li><a href=\"#blog-53-section-3\">Support implementation and verification</a></li><li><a href=\"#blog-53-section-4\">Explain progress in business context</a></li></ol></nav><div class=\"blog-prose\"><p>Rankings can help describe search visibility, but they do not explain the whole role of an SEO specialist. A useful programme connects the website's discoverability and content with the questions customers ask and the actions the business wants to support.</p>\n<p>Ask how the specialist moves from research to changes on the live site. The answer should make the work understandable to writers, developers and the people responsible for customer enquiries.</p>\n<h2 id=\"blog-53-section-1\">Understand the offer and audience</h2>\n<p>The specialist should learn what the business provides, where it operates and which customers fit. Intent research becomes more useful when it reflects those details. A large collection of related keywords still needs judgement before it becomes a plan.</p>\n<p>For an illustrative local provider, search activity from an unsuitable location may contribute little to the commercial goal. The research should distinguish that activity from relevant demand rather than celebrate the combined traffic total.</p>\n<h2 id=\"blog-53-section-2\">Review the technical and content foundations</h2>\n<p>Inspect the priority pages and the way the site connects them. Identify issues affecting access, interpretation or the visitor's experience. Explain findings with examples and propose changes that the team can review.</p>\n<p>Content work should improve the answer a page provides. A specialist may identify that a service is poorly explained, that related pages lack a clear distinction or that useful guidance has no natural link to the relevant offer.</p>\n<h2 id=\"blog-53-section-3\">Support implementation and verification</h2>\n<p>Recommendations need owners and a route into delivery. Clarify who writes, builds, approves and checks the work. After release, confirm that the live page reflects the intended change and that important functionality still works.</p>\n<p>Keep an implementation record so the team can interpret later movement. A completed fix and an observed search result are different pieces of evidence, and the report should preserve that distinction.</p>\n<h2 id=\"blog-53-section-4\">Explain progress in business context</h2>\n<p>Review relevant visibility and website activity alongside enquiries where the data supports it. State comparison periods and discuss customer-fit feedback. A ranking improvement is more informative when the business understands the question, page and audience involved.</p>\n<p>Fyntix's SEO service combines technical foundations, research, content structure and reporting. A useful specialist helps those responsibilities work together, producing a clearer website and a practical sequence of improvements. Rankings have a place in the review, alongside the information needed to decide what the business should do next.</p></div><aside class=\"blog-service-callout\" aria-label=\"Work with Fyntix\"><p class=\"blog-eyebrow\">Put the idea into practice</p><h2>Plan your next step with Fyntix.</h2><p>Connect your audience and offer with a practical plan for search visibility, paid media and useful content.</p><div class=\"blog-callout-links\"><a href=\"/contact\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-full\">Book a free strategy call</a><a href=\"/services#service-seo\">Explore the relevant service</a></div></aside></article></section></div>"
